ow  but obviously there's an estrogen surge  remember breast feeding in this study  had no protective effect in either  direction at all was a protective and  didn't cause risk but the estrogen surge  may cause breast cancer to prevent  earlier that's a hypothesis it certainly  hasn't been proven yet and if you have a  breast cancer history in your family  what about if you want to have a child  well in this case having a breast cancer  history or not didn't matter  in this study if you have a breast  cancer history you're at a higher risk  of breast cancer obviously you need to  be screened closer but this study  doesn't affect that and would you advise  women to do anything differently yeah I  want them to talk to the doctor and say  listen I have my last child at an older  age so maybe I should be screened  earlier because my risk is going to be  highest five years out from that point  so the discussion with the doctor is  critical to bring in this information  all right dr. David egg is always good  to have you thank you so much thank you  an important point to make as women are  having children later in life and so  starting to get our baseline at age 40  yes talk to your doctor
 

